{"id": "00a664612b574242b61486af338bbafc", "query": "Given a large integer N (up to 1e6), find the maximum number of distinct binary strings of length N that can be formed such that no two strings are identical and no string is a prefix of another string? Can we use a sliding window approach to find a subsequence in a string such that the sum of characters in the subsequence is divisible by a given number? What is the maximum number of non-overlapping rectangles that can be formed using a set of N points in a 2D plane, given that each point is represented by an integer coordinate x and y, and each rectangle must have a width and height of at least a and b respectively, where a and b are given integers? What is the maximum number of non-overlapping rectangles that can be formed?", "raw_text": " Can we solve these using dynamic programming?\n---------------------------------------------------\n\n---------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT\n---------------------------------------------------\n===START_JSON===\n{\n  \"explicit_dimensions\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"distinct_binary_strings\",\n      \"value\": \"max(N choose N/2) = max(binomial_coefficient(N, N/2))\",\n      \"justification\": \"The problem asks for the maximum number of distinct binary strings of length N that do not share prefixes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"prefix_avoidance_constraint\",\n      \"value\": \"no two strings are identical and no string is a prefix of another string\",\n      \"justification\": \"Explicitly stated constraint requiring uniqueness and prefix avoidance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"binary_length\",\n      \"value\": \"N\",\n      \"justification\": \"Input size is fixed at N (up to 1e6).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"missed_dimensions\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"sliding_window_sum_divisible_by_k\",\n      \"value\": [\"positive integers k; any k >= 1\"],\n      \"justification\": \"Sliding window sum divisibility constraint implies considering sums modulo some positive divisor k, which could impact choice of DP states and algorithms.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"non_overlapping_rectangles\",\n      \"value\": [\"2D coordinates; a,b >= 0; rectangular bounds defined by min(x1,x2,...) <= left < right <= max(x1,x2,...); min(y1,y2,...) <= bottom < top <= max(y1,y2,...); a and b define minimum width and height\"],\n      \"justification\": \"The problem involves counting non-overlapping rectangles over a set of points under area constraints a and b.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"dynamic_programming_feasibility\",\n      \"value\": [\"DP state space depends on constraints; consider storing pairs of indices per axis; need a recurrence based on overlap checks; optimization via memoization or pruning likely\"],\n      \"justification\": \"Dynamic programming might require encoding rectangle overlaps and using memoized transitions; feasibility hinges on precise DP state design.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"point_representation_type\",\n      \"value\": [\"integer coordinates (x,y) per point; e.g., integers within [left, right] and [bottom,top]\"],\n      \"justification\": \"Coordinates are represented as integers; algorithm should handle numeric ranges and boundaries.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"feasible_rectangle_bounds\",\n      \"value\": [\"existence of valid rectangles requires left <= right and bottom <= top; a <= width <= right-left and b <= height <= top-bottom; valid regions depend on axis-aligned bounds\"],\n      \"justification\": \"Valid rectangles must fit within grid bounds and satisfy width and height constraints; algorithm needs to filter candidate rectangles against these bounds.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n===END_JSON===\n\nPlease note that the explicit dimensions describe what the user explicitly mentions, while the missed dimensions capture important aspects not explicitly stated but crucial for designing a correct solution. The latter includes key details about the problem structure, constraints, and algorithmic implications that a typical competitor would consider when tackling these types of questions. The output aims to guide further analysis and provide insights into potential approaches and corner cases that might be overlooked.", "json_data": {"explicit_dimensions": [{"name": "distinct_binary_strings", "value": "max(N choose N/2) = max(binomial_coefficient(N, N/2))", "justification": "The problem asks for the maximum number of distinct binary strings of length N that do not share prefixes."}, {"name": "prefix_avoidance_constraint", "value": "no two strings are identical and no string is a prefix of another string", "justification": "Explicitly stated constraint requiring uniqueness and prefix avoidance."}, {"name": "binary_length", "value": "N", "justification": "Input size is fixed at N (up to 1e6)."}], "implicit_dimensions": [{"name": "sliding_window_sum_divisible_by_k", "value": ["positive integers k; any k >= 1"], "justification": "Sliding window sum divisibility constraint implies considering sums modulo some positive divisor k, which could impact choice of DP states and algorithms."}, {"name": "non_overlapping_rectangles", "value": ["2D coordinates; a,b >= 0; rectangular bounds defined by min(x1,x2,...) <= left < right <= max(x1,x2,...); min(y1,y2,...) <= bottom < top <= max(y1,y2,...); a and b define minimum width and height"], "justification": "The problem involves counting non-overlapping rectangles over a set of points under area constraints a and b."}, {"name": "dynamic_programming_feasibility", "value": ["DP state space depends on constraints; consider storing pairs of indices per axis; need a recurrence based on overlap checks; optimization via memoization or pruning likely"], "justification": "Dynamic programming might require encoding rectangle overlaps and using memoized transitions; feasibility hinges on precise DP state design."}, {"name": "point_representation_type", "value": ["integer coordinates (x,y) per point; 